0 !HISTORY 2015-10-06 {Roland Melkert} Initial info for stud4.dat

0 //NOTE: Needs multi matching feature to prevent unwanted snapping when combined with e.g. plates.
0 //      when available all parts using it need to be revisited as those currently have their own info if usefull (e.g. minifig hats).
0 //!LDCAD SNAP_CYL [id=aStud] [gender=F] [caps=one] [secs=R 6 4]

0 //Added by StudLab (by-hand-add)

0 //The tube under a brick, where a single stud fits (the shadow library's stud4.dat has it commented out, until
0 //LDCad can match several connections at once; StudLab's snapping prefers places with more studs). Closed at the
0 //primitive's origin, which parts put at the top of the tube, as the library's stud4o.dat has it.
0 !LDCAD SNAP_CYL [id=aStud] [gender=F] [caps=A] [secs=R 6 4] [scale=YOnly]
